        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Capture unit identity: OEM, model, serial, engine number, hour-meter baseline, photos, and any VIN/registration.
Responsible (R): Mechanic
Accountable (A): Rental Fleet Manager
Duration: 1 hour</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5324_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5324_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5324_Task8" name="Install telematics/IoT unit (GPS, hour-meter feed, geofence, kill-switch where…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Install telematics/IoT unit (GPS, hour-meter feed, geofence, kill-switch where fitted).
Responsible (R): IT/IoT Engineer
Accountable (A): Rental Fleet Manager
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5324_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5324_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5324_Task9" name="Register the unit in the Rental Fleet module as a unique rentable asset with…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Register the unit in the Rental Fleet module as a unique rentable asset with utilization/maintenance counters.
Responsible (R): Rental Fleet Manager
Accountable (A): Rental Fleet Manager
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5324_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5324_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5324_Task10" name="Link telematics feed to the ERP rental-lifecycle events (pickup, return…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Link telematics feed to the ERP rental-lifecycle events (pickup, return, geofence breach).
Responsible (R): IT/IoT Engineer
Accountable (A): Rental Fleet Manager
Duration: 1 hour</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5324_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5324_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
